Package: NMSDE
Type: Package
Title: Nonparametric Multivariate Spectral Density Estimation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Shirin", "Nezampour", email = "sh.nezampour@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Mehdi", "Maadooliat", email = "mehdi.maadooliat@marquette.edu", role = "aut"))
Description: Nonparametric estimation of spectral density matrices of
    multivariate stationary time series. The inverse spectral matrix is
    parameterized through its complex Cholesky factor, whose components are
    expanded in a B-spline basis and estimated by minimizing a penalized
    Whittle likelihood with Newton-Raphson iterations, which guarantees
    Hermitian positive-definite estimates (Nezampour et al., 2024)
    <doi:10.1007/s00180-023-01451-4>. For a collection of multivariate time
    series, the Cholesky components are assumed to lie in a common
    low-dimensional subspace, giving collective estimates that borrow
    strength across series and can be used to cluster the series in the
    frequency domain, extending Maadooliat et al. (2018) <doi:10.1002/sim.7972>
    to the multivariate setting. The smoothing parameter can be updated
    within the iterations, and spectral bootstrap confidence intervals and an
    interactive 'shiny' application are provided.
